{
  "functions": [
    "PlatformHttpClient.send"
  ],
  "description": "PlatformHttpClient against a small HTTP/1.1 server the test runs on 127.0.0.1 (plan §9 HttpClient): URLSession, HttpClient, libsoup. The server's routes: /echo answers 200 with the JSON {method, path, header (the X-Test request header, or null), body (the request body as text)}; /status/<n> answers <n> with the body 'status <n>'; /slow waits 5 s, then answers 200. given.url's <server> is the server's address (http://127.0.0.1:<port>); <closed> is a port nothing listens on. Any status is an answer; no answer is http.failed with the system's reason; a cancelled call is job.cancelled.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "get-echo",
      "given": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "<server>/echo",
        "headers": {
          "X-Test": "one"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/echo",
          "header": "one",
          "body": ""
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "post-body",
      "given": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "<server>/echo",
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"a\":1}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/echo",
          "header": null,
          "body": "{\"a\":1}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "any-status-is-an-answer",
      "given": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "<server>/status/503"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 503,
        "text": "status 503"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "no-answer",
      "given": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "<closed>/echo"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error": "http.failed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cancelled",
      "given": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "<server>/slow",
        "cancelAfter": 0.3
      },
      "expect": {
        "error": "job.cancelled",
        "within": 3
      }
    }
  ]
}
